# Terminal (Windows)

When the host shell is Windows PowerShell:

- MUST chain commands with `;`, not `&&` (example: `cd path; git status`).
- Prefer absolute paths; MUST quote paths that contain spaces.
- MUST remove directories with `Remove-Item -Recurse` (not `rmdir /s`).
- If script execution is disabled: run `Set-ExecutionPolicy -ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser`, or use cmd.exe.
